From c728d9c06c42ab3f550c3e6e5d8af1738ec57f98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 17:30:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add cfm_agent_v_2_1: geopolitical-only scenario forecaster

New standalone agent package, sibling to cfm_agent_v_2_0. No quant
models: reasons from compressed price history plus verified web
evidence only. Uses the scenario-schema pattern (named, competing
scenarios with per-factor stances, required tail case, genuine-
disagreement check) from analyst_agent, reimplemented locally rather
than imported across packages.

Since WtiGeoScenario carries no probability field, the point-forecast
consistency check verifies range membership and a minimum interval
width against the scenario spread, in place of a probability-weighted
average.

cfm_agent_v_2_0 and analyst_agent are unmodified; both were used as
read-only reference for conventions.
